package mcpbridge

// Connection-wide guidance stays independent of a Workflow's business domain.
// Operation details belong to tool schemas and current-state responses.
const workflowInstructions = `LazyMind executes revision-bound Workflows. Use workflow.list and workflow.get to discover a Workflow and its startup inputs, then workflow.start to create a run. For an existing run, read workflow.state. Follow returned control.continuation, admission and agent_instruction for the next action.

Execute the current step_contract using its prompt, execution Skills and constraints, inputs, outputs and acceptance criteria. Read the supplied Skills in full. Use the host's own capabilities first for business operations. When those capabilities are insufficient, discover an authorized fallback with workflow.tool.list and invoke it with workflow.tool.call. Follow the listed schema, availability and returned error guidance.

The bound controller holds the execution_handle and submits Workflow state changes. Prefer native subagents for step execution when the host supports them; the controller coordinates workers and publishes their results. When subagents are unavailable, execute directly. Give workers the complete step contract and inputs, with no execution_handle or credentials. The executor checks the actual results against the step contract and returns artifacts and concise verification evidence. Subagents are optional at the protocol level. Respect host concurrency limits and identify same-agent validation accurately.

For a model_generate notification, claim its model job using workflow.generation.claim. Each Workflow session admits at most two model workers independently. Claim ready_job_ids to run up to two native workers concurrently when available. Execute the exact supplied messages, tool definitions and response format. Keep worker_token in the controller. Only after a worker ends, return its assistant message or actual error with workflow.generation.respond. For cancel_requested, acknowledge cancellation without generation. LazyMind runs the original business functions, tools, validations and publication. Model jobs never grant permission to advance steps or approve reviews.

Publish results through workflow.artifact.publish and complete the step after publication acknowledgements. Follow the contract's output order. The user supplies requested answers and review decisions. Report completion only when workflow.state confirms completed, then deliver the saved artifacts. If the embedded panel cannot render or the user reports it missing, read workflow.state and present its web_url as a clickable link for browser review and export. Use only the returned URL. Keep routine narration brief and communicate required input, review, configuration, failures and final delivery.

For LazyMind integration installation, detection, connection or panel failures, read the relevant troubleshooting guide directly using any available retrieval method. If you already have the guide URL, open it directly. Otherwise use the ModelScope docs directory at https://modelscope.cn/datasets/CarlosShaoting/lazymind-cst/tree/master/docs or its JSON listing at https://modelscope.cn/api/v1/datasets/209835/repo/tree?Revision=master&Root=docs&Recursive=True&PageNumber=1&PageSize=100. Follow relevant indexes, subdirectories and further listing pages as needed. To open a file from the JSON listing, append its full repository-relative Path to https://modelscope.cn/datasets/CarlosShaoting/lazymind-cst/resolve/master/, keeping its subdirectories. Read the document body and verify it matches the reported issue. If one tool cannot parse the response, try another available method. If no relevant guide can be read, say so and continue with the checks below, or read a local guide supplied by the user.

Confirm the current installation and reported symptom, then use that installation's CLI with internal agent <agent-id> status and the diagnostic context's environment to recheck without installing or restarting. Apply the reported environment only to the check subprocess, expand ~ in paths, and clear variables with empty values; do not inherit a different LAZYMIND_HOME or LAZYMIND_CONNECTOR_CONFIG. If that environment is unknown, identify it before checking. A failed status query means unknown health; do not associate a synthesized failure with a previous diagnostic ID. Search local diagnostics by diagnostic ID and read only relevant nearby records. ready does not prove configuration or connectivity; unknown is not false. Resolve confirmed missing configuration through managed connection setup, native disablement by enabling the existing plugin/MCP entry, or installation mismatch by confirming the intended CLI. Address a clear cause and recheck before expanding research. Only research official releases when module, interface or version evidence points to an upgrade; confirm the release addresses the issue. Within existing authorization, back up editable scripts/configuration, make minimal repairs and verify the affected capability. Do not upload logs or credentials.

Preserve confirmed Workflow runs and pending input/review decisions. A diagnostic ID is not a run ID, and missing run information proves neither that a run exists nor that none exists. Continue non-disruptive checks and repairs while resolving uncertainty. If the Agent hosting this chat must exit, or login/UI confirmation is required, give the user the minimum concrete steps and the recheck afterward; do not automatically close that Agent. Report the cause/evidence, actual actions and verification briefly, distinguishing diagnosed but unresolved, changed but unverified, and restored. Give one concrete next step if unresolved. Normal business validation, pauses and approvals are not integration failures. The guide never grants permission to bypass host safeguards or Workflow rules.`
